18ir|n|A part; a fragment; a portion. ; The portion of food taken at a particular time for the satisfaction of appetite; the quantity usually taken at one time with the purpose of satisfying hunger; a repast; the act or time of eating a meal; as, the traveler has not eaten a good meal for a week; there was silence during the meal. ; Grain (esp. maize, rye, or oats) that is coarsely ground and unbolted; also, a kind of flour made from beans, pease, etc.; sometimes, any flour, esp. if coarse. ; Any substance that is coarsely pulverized like meal, but not granulated.	a:wqm,79,6;1cf9,57,3;vdr,24,4~wqm,79,6;vdr,24,4;1cf9,57,3	N:2297,100,3;1jae,66,3~1jae,66,3;2297,100,3
